Enhancement: Speed up `backup` with many exclude patterns

Restic checked every exclude pattern against every file and directory it
visited, both while scanning and while backing up. Patterns containing `**`
were tried at every depth of a path, so long exclude lists could take most of
the time of a backup with few changes: on a Windows system drive with 273
patterns, matching took about 300 seconds of CPU time for 744,000 paths.

Restic now first checks whether a path contains the plain text a pattern
requires, such as the folder name in `**/node_modules/` or the `.tmp` in
`*.tmp`, and skips the pattern otherwise. In the example above, matching now
takes about 7 seconds. Which files are excluded or included is unchanged.

